    "description": {
      "value": "<p>Your companion is a corpulent toad with bony horns fused to resemble a crown.</p><p><strong>Size</strong> Small</p><p><strong>Melee</strong> <span class=\"pf2-icon\">1</span> tongue (agile, reach 10 feet), Damage 1d6 bludgeoning</p><p><strong>Str</strong> +2, <strong>Dex</strong> +2, <strong>Con</strong> +3, <strong>Int</strong> –4, <strong>Wis</strong> +1, <strong>Cha</strong> +0</p><p><strong>Hit Points</strong> 8</p><p><strong>Skill</strong> Survival</p><p><strong>Speed</strong> 20 feet, burrow 10 feet</p><p><strong>Support Benefit</strong> Your regal toad puffs itself up like a balloon. Until the start of your next turn, your regal toad provides cover as though it were Huge (this is usually standard cover for Medium creatures). It still occupies the same space.</p><p><strong>Advanced Maneuver</strong> @UUID[Compendium.pf2e-animal-companions.sf-AC-Advanced-Maneuvers.Item.Mtc8ep0VRdbTNSL5]{Bellowing Croak}</p><p></p>",
